6. Backend Development
The backend acts as the bridge between the frontend, Gemini, database, and other services.
Frontend
    │
    ▼
Backend API
    │
    ├── Gemini Service
    ├── Database Service
    ├── Authentication
    └── Asset Service
The frontend should not directly expose secret API credentials.
________________________________________
7. Gemini Integration
The Gemini service receives structured information from the backend.
Example request concept
Generate a comic story.

Genre: Science Fiction
Tone: Adventure
Length: 8 panels

Story idea:
A teenager discovers an abandoned robot
in a futuristic city.

Return:
1. Title
2. Synopsis
3. Characters
4. Scenes
5. Panel descriptions
6. Dialogue
The backend then validates and stores the response.
________________________________________
8. Structured AI Output
Instead of relying on free-form text, ComicCraft should request structured output.
Example:
{
  "title": "The Lost Robot",
  "synopsis": "...",
  "characters": [
    {
      "name": "Arun",
      "role": "Protagonist",
      "personality": "Curious and brave"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "scene": "...",
      "dialogue": "...",
      "narration": "..."
    }
  ]
}
This makes the generated content easier for the application to display and edit.
