Conclusion
The ComicCraft development should be implemented incrementally, beginning with the core prompt-to-story functionality and then extending it to characters, scenes, panels, dialogue, artwork, editing, and export. A structured data model and modular Gemini service are particularly important because they allow individual parts of a comic to be regenerated without losing the rest of the user's work.

